Harbor: Windows.Foundation.Uri answers for its parts (#95).

A Uri made by iertutil kept the text it was created from and answered only RawUri (and AbsoluteUri with the
same text); Host, SchemeName, Path, Query, Port and the rest returned E_NOTIMPL. Office's web add-in host
takes an add-in's address apart this way before it starts the web view.

The parts now come from urlmon's CreateUri, which already implements the parsing. urlmon is loaded when a Uri
is first asked for a part, so iertutil doesn't pull it into every process. A part the address doesn't have is
the empty string and Port is 0, as on Windows. Suspicious is always FALSE. QueryParsed, Equals and CombineUri
are unchanged.

Test: WindowsTests/winrt.

